.page read 1 read a line into variables

# SYNOPSIS
*read* [*-r*] [*-p* _PROMPT_] [_NAME_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`read` is a gapsh builtin. It reads one line from standard input, splits it at blanks and assigns the words to the _NAME_s in order; the last name takes the rest of the line. With no name the line goes to `REPLY`. A backslash at the end of the line joins the next line unless `-r` is given, which also stops backslashes from quoting anything.

# OPTIONS
@ *-r*
    Do not treat backslash specially.
@ *-p* _PROMPT_
    Write _PROMPT_ on standard error first.

# EXIT STATUS
0 if a line was read, 1 at the end of the input.

# EXAMPLES
    read -p "name? " who
    while read a b; do echo "$b $a"; done < pairs.txt

# SEE ALSO
gapsh-language(7), cat(1)
